1
00:00:07,801 --> 00:00:09,202
(All characters, places, and organizations
in this drama are fictitious.)

2
00:00:09,227 --> 00:00:10,730
(Filming followed broadcast guidelines
for minors, some scenes used AI.)

3
00:00:12,095 --> 00:00:14,002
(Episode 21)

4
00:00:29,976 --> 00:00:31,797
Where is Gyu Rim?

5
00:00:39,378 --> 00:00:40,791
Mu Jin!

6
00:01:06,044 --> 00:01:07,885
It's me, Gyu Rim.

7
00:01:17,213 --> 00:01:18,443
Tiger.

8
00:01:29,491 --> 00:01:31,532
I got a week off.

9
00:01:32,704 --> 00:01:35,906
I suddenly had a craving for your pasta.

10
00:01:37,211 --> 00:01:39,747
Well, I'm glad you came.

11
00:01:41,058 --> 00:01:43,157
What's the best thing here?

12
00:01:43,517 --> 00:01:45,551
What should I have, Mu Jin?

13
00:01:46,618 --> 00:01:49,785
We got some great vongole in today.
Want me to make that?

14
00:01:50,804 --> 00:01:52,363
What's vongole?

15
00:01:54,538 --> 00:01:55,911
Clams.

16
00:01:59,845 --> 00:02:01,840
See? I'm so clueless.

17
00:02:07,105 --> 00:02:10,661
- I'm so ignorant it's embarrassing.
- No, you're not.

18
00:02:11,204 --> 00:02:13,629
But just because my boyfriend
is an Italian chef,

19
00:02:13,654 --> 00:02:15,923
it's not like I have to know
what vongole means.

20
00:02:16,801 --> 00:02:19,055
Of course not.
You don't need to know that.

21
00:02:20,065 --> 00:02:22,652
Want me to make you a plate of clam pasta?

22
00:02:23,591 --> 00:02:26,832
Yes. Make it extra delicious.

23
00:02:27,555 --> 00:02:28,637
Okay.

24
00:02:48,331 --> 00:02:49,951
Boil just 80 grams of linguine for me.

25
00:02:49,976 --> 00:02:51,850
- I'm making vongole pasta.
- Yes, Chef.

26
00:03:24,743 --> 00:03:26,618
What's wrong with Han Gyu Rim?

27
00:03:27,632 --> 00:03:29,070
She's lost it, right?

28
00:03:30,564 --> 00:03:31,931
Is she on something?

29
00:03:32,911 --> 00:03:35,266
The customers all know
that bizarre woman is your...

30
00:03:36,526 --> 00:03:39,959
girlfriend, and they're all
whispering about it right now.

31
00:03:40,285 --> 00:03:42,085
You're really getting humiliated today...

32
00:03:42,110 --> 00:03:45,355
Bizarre? She just looks pretty.

33
00:03:45,955 --> 00:03:47,648
You said you were scared of tigers.

34
00:03:48,323 --> 00:03:49,889
In the name of restaurant policy,

35
00:03:49,914 --> 00:03:54,085
you banned couples and married people
and made this a couple-free zone,

36
00:03:54,265 --> 00:03:58,105
so why let your girlfriend in
and go on dates here?

37
00:03:58,130 --> 00:04:00,404
Of course the customers are talking.

38
00:04:16,380 --> 00:04:17,380
(No couples allowed)

39
00:04:17,405 --> 00:04:18,405
(Da Solo welcomes solo diners,
friends, and family gatherings)

40
00:04:37,678 --> 00:04:40,948
Looks delicious. Thank you.

41
00:04:42,078 --> 00:04:45,071
Enjoy your meal.

42
00:05:06,251 --> 00:05:09,842
Did we give you the spoon and knife
to take home with you?

43
00:05:14,643 --> 00:05:16,120
What do I do?

44
00:05:19,668 --> 00:05:21,145
This is bad.

45
00:05:22,325 --> 00:05:26,452
I think clam sauce dripped on it.

46
00:05:30,116 --> 00:05:33,736
Is she putting her shoe on the table
to wipe it?

47
00:05:33,774 --> 00:05:36,711
I'm so upset.

48
00:05:39,643 --> 00:05:45,027
You can't put your shoe
on a table where people eat.

49
00:05:45,944 --> 00:05:48,404
And wiping it with a napkin
meant for your mouth, too.

50
00:05:48,429 --> 00:05:49,884
I'll wipe my mouth with it too.

51
00:05:55,865 --> 00:05:58,525
I think clam sauce got on my shoe.

52
00:05:58,651 --> 00:06:01,096
I paid a lot to rent these.

53
00:06:01,121 --> 00:06:04,328
It won't come off. What do I do?

54
00:06:14,284 --> 00:06:15,903
I'll get your shoes cleaned.

55
00:06:18,112 --> 00:06:21,463
Tell them to throw this napkin away
when they clear the table.

56
00:06:22,845 --> 00:06:25,299
I'll cover everyone's meal today.

57
00:06:25,324 --> 00:06:28,008
I apologize if you were offended.

58
00:06:33,885 --> 00:06:35,355
I'll bring you a fresh plate.

59
00:06:35,380 --> 00:06:36,996
Want to eat outside?

60
00:06:41,077 --> 00:06:42,077
Okay.

61
00:06:54,597 --> 00:06:58,041
- You're embarrassed by me, aren't you?
- No.

62
00:07:03,478 --> 00:07:06,826
Sit. I'll set up a glass
and utensils in a minute.

63
00:07:08,784 --> 00:07:11,671
"Who even acts like this?"
You're embarrassed by me.

64
00:07:12,918 --> 00:07:16,163
That's why you didn't charge the customers
and brought me out here.

65
00:07:18,165 --> 00:07:21,135
I came out because I wanted to be
alone with you, just the two of us.

66
00:07:21,698 --> 00:07:23,303
Without worrying about other people.

67
00:07:45,718 --> 00:07:47,198
You're a little...

68
00:07:49,071 --> 00:07:51,801
No, you know you're acting
really strange today, right?

69
00:07:52,370 --> 00:07:55,667
The way you're acting, the way you look.

70
00:07:57,784 --> 00:08:02,394
I'm really thrown, so could you bring back
the Han Gyu Rim I know?

71
00:08:03,598 --> 00:08:05,058
This is the real me.

72
00:08:06,565 --> 00:08:08,919
I'm a nutcase who makes
Han Gyu Yeong look tame.

73
00:08:09,417 --> 00:08:11,151
I just never let it show.

74
00:08:14,485 --> 00:08:18,965
I was watching TV yesterday,
and some philosopher said,

75
00:08:19,465 --> 00:08:21,626
"Don't take life too seriously."

76
00:08:22,705 --> 00:08:24,858
"Nobody gets out alive anyway."

77
00:08:28,450 --> 00:08:31,247
It hit me like a bolt of lightning.

78
00:08:32,140 --> 00:08:36,251
Right. Life is something
nobody gets out of alive anyway,

79
00:08:36,405 --> 00:08:41,451
so why was I so serious, so strict,
so worried about what people think,

80
00:08:41,505 --> 00:08:44,011
pretending to be a good girl all the time?

81
00:08:45,671 --> 00:08:51,869
So it's a little late, but from now on,
no more faking, no more hypocrisy.

82
00:08:52,598 --> 00:08:54,469
I'll do whatever I want,

83
00:08:54,570 --> 00:08:57,436
eat whatever I want, wear whatever I want,

84
00:08:59,308 --> 00:09:04,865
and live the way my heart
and my desires tell me to.

85
00:09:06,417 --> 00:09:07,949
Okay, I get it.

86
00:09:08,875 --> 00:09:14,982
I get what you're thinking
and how determined you are.

87
00:09:16,978 --> 00:09:19,036
I've been wondering about something.

88
00:09:19,256 --> 00:09:23,236
So is this look what your desires want?

89
00:09:23,604 --> 00:09:26,037
Is this what your heart is telling you?

90
00:09:30,197 --> 00:09:32,429
Yes. Totally.

91
00:09:36,064 --> 00:09:41,470
Actually, there's an outfit
I've had my eye on for a few days,

92
00:09:42,418 --> 00:09:45,111
but it's a bit out of my budget.

93
00:09:47,344 --> 00:09:50,710
Could you buy it for me, Mu Jin?

94
00:10:02,579 --> 00:10:04,503
Poop brown doesn't suit me.

95
00:10:04,637 --> 00:10:07,211
Cash would've been better.

96
00:10:07,278 --> 00:10:09,482
Hey, your mother-in-law is the best.

97
00:10:09,558 --> 00:10:11,450
Sending you gifts like this.

98
00:10:11,764 --> 00:10:13,919
She gave you diamond earrings too, right?

99
00:10:15,171 --> 00:10:17,211
She must have a guilty conscience.

100
00:10:17,236 --> 00:10:19,662
Guilty about what? Did something happen?

101
00:10:20,665 --> 00:10:23,194
It's such a hassle to exchange it.

102
00:10:24,411 --> 00:10:27,059
How much could I get for this on Karrot?

103
00:10:34,584 --> 00:10:36,359
I'm going to see Cho Heung Sik.

104
00:10:36,445 --> 00:10:39,267
To find out in person
what's going on between you two.

105
00:10:39,372 --> 00:10:42,012
Why would you see him? To get beaten up?

106
00:10:42,037 --> 00:10:44,709
I told you it's nothing like that,
you idiot!

107
00:10:44,763 --> 00:10:47,397
Are you having an affair or something?

108
00:10:50,990 --> 00:10:52,885
Have lunch without me. I'll be right back.

109
00:10:54,240 --> 00:10:55,814
Don't touch it.

110
00:10:57,238 --> 00:10:59,242
You said you two are relatives.

111
00:11:00,038 --> 00:11:02,132
So prove it.

112
00:11:03,981 --> 00:11:07,209
You're a cheater, and you're paranoid
about your wife on top of it?

113
00:11:07,623 --> 00:11:09,863
You're really something else.

114
00:11:10,148 --> 00:11:12,281
You two are having an affair!

115
00:11:16,915 --> 00:11:18,881
It's not an affair.

116
00:11:19,281 --> 00:11:22,648
If it's not, then prove it.

117
00:11:23,448 --> 00:11:26,115
How do I prove something isn't true
when it isn't?

118
00:11:26,415 --> 00:11:29,448
Then you prove Gyu Yeong and I
are having an affair.

119
00:11:29,481 --> 00:11:30,841
I said you prove it.

120
00:11:30,888 --> 00:11:33,656
You lied and said you're relatives
when you're not.

121
00:11:33,681 --> 00:11:37,315
We are relatives.
We're both descendants of Dangun.

122
00:11:39,515 --> 00:11:41,548
See? I knew it was an affair.

123
00:11:41,581 --> 00:11:45,681
Hey, out of all the women out there,
you go for a woman with a husband...

124
00:11:45,848 --> 00:11:52,381
This is driving me nuts.
I'm going to lose my mind, seriously.

125
00:11:54,081 --> 00:11:57,315
What do I do with these two?
Should I report them to the police?

126
00:11:57,348 --> 00:11:59,148
Or post them both on the internet...

127
00:12:03,815 --> 00:12:05,215
Why'd you hit me?

128
00:12:05,248 --> 00:12:06,980
You're the one who's cheating!

129
00:12:07,020 --> 00:12:09,167
Did you come here to show off
what a lunatic you are?

130
00:12:09,248 --> 00:12:10,907
What did I tell you?

131
00:12:11,091 --> 00:12:13,924
Didn't I say you can't marry
a guy like this?

132
00:12:15,248 --> 00:12:17,281
He tried to stop our wedding?

133
00:12:17,681 --> 00:12:20,848
- You're asking for it...
- I'll kill you.

134
00:12:22,481 --> 00:12:27,948
You never listened to me and stubbornly
had your way. Serves you right.

135
00:12:28,515 --> 00:12:31,081
If you've seen enough,
end it right now and...

136
00:12:31,081 --> 00:12:32,481
I'm not getting a divorce.

137
00:12:33,581 --> 00:12:34,615
Gyu Yeong.

138
00:12:34,748 --> 00:12:38,640
Right, Gyu Yeong.
Why would we get divorced?

139
00:12:38,665 --> 00:12:41,474
We just need to get rid of
this home-wrecking jerk.

140
00:12:44,281 --> 00:12:46,005
It's not an affair.

141
00:12:46,106 --> 00:12:48,756
What you're doing right now
is the real affair.

142
00:12:48,781 --> 00:12:51,148
I'm telling you to quit everything
and go back to your family.

143
00:12:51,181 --> 00:12:53,248
I told you I'm not getting a divorce.

144
00:12:55,048 --> 00:12:59,281
Right, Gyu Yeong.
Let's never get divorced.

145
00:12:59,881 --> 00:13:05,215
Right, let's not get divorced,
and just date other people on our own.

146
00:13:05,415 --> 00:13:07,848
- What?
- What are you even saying?

147
00:13:07,881 --> 00:13:10,215
I told you if you cheat,
I'll cheat right back.

148
00:13:14,002 --> 00:13:18,125
You seem to be alone. If you're free,
how about having an affair with me?

149
00:13:19,815 --> 00:13:21,442
Sure, why not?

150
00:13:23,815 --> 00:13:25,581
Say something.

151
00:13:28,248 --> 00:13:31,481
Ta-da. How do I look? So pretty, right?

152
00:13:33,348 --> 00:13:35,015
I wanted to wear this. What do you think?

153
00:13:37,265 --> 00:13:38,381
You don't like it?

154
00:13:40,481 --> 00:13:44,084
I think yellow looks good on me, right?
I love it.

155
00:13:44,752 --> 00:13:46,315
Mu Jin.

156
00:13:51,581 --> 00:13:54,115
- Hey.
- What?

157
00:14:00,148 --> 00:14:04,681
Mu Jin, what do you think? Pretty, right?

158
00:14:07,348 --> 00:14:08,881
I love it.

159
00:14:11,948 --> 00:14:13,548
How about this?

160
00:14:26,881 --> 00:14:30,015
Ta-da, how do I look?

161
00:14:35,681 --> 00:14:39,915
Isn't it cool? Super cool, right?

162
00:14:39,940 --> 00:14:41,656
I think this kind of look suits me.

163
00:14:43,040 --> 00:14:44,619
I'm tired.

164
00:14:45,848 --> 00:14:47,548
- Tired, right?
- Yeah.

165
00:14:48,967 --> 00:14:50,115
You're sweating.

166
00:14:55,015 --> 00:14:57,115
Which outfit do you like best, Mu Jin?

167
00:14:58,415 --> 00:15:03,981
Isn't this a little too flashy
to wear every day?

168
00:15:04,615 --> 00:15:07,681
I feel like it would look good
on a girl group onstage.

169
00:15:07,815 --> 00:15:10,181
So unless I'm in a girl group,
I can't wear what I want?

170
00:15:11,748 --> 00:15:14,626
- That's not what I meant...
- This is my style.

171
00:15:15,048 --> 00:15:17,248
This is exactly my style.

172
00:15:18,048 --> 00:15:19,048
Okay...

173
00:15:19,515 --> 00:15:20,815
You'll buy me all of these, right?

174
00:15:21,181 --> 00:15:22,781
You're going to wear all of these?

175
00:15:23,048 --> 00:15:25,148
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

176
00:15:25,748 --> 00:15:28,281
I'll take everything I tried on today.

177
00:15:28,515 --> 00:15:30,248
My boyfriend's buying them for me.

178
00:15:30,915 --> 00:15:32,181
Of course.

179
00:15:34,781 --> 00:15:38,038
- Thank you, Mu Jin.
- Sure.

180
00:16:15,413 --> 00:16:18,703
Hey.

181
00:16:33,094 --> 00:16:34,127
Gyu O.

182
00:16:36,981 --> 00:16:41,178
Please, just this once, let it go.

183
00:16:41,679 --> 00:16:43,472
If not for me, then for my kid...

184
00:16:46,181 --> 00:16:50,553
Come on, if both parents have records,
what happens to my kid's life?

185
00:16:51,480 --> 00:16:53,006
Please, Gyu O.

186
00:16:56,915 --> 00:16:59,115
I really didn't know, okay?

187
00:17:00,015 --> 00:17:02,848
My wife and your manager
did it together behind my back.

188
00:17:03,581 --> 00:17:08,581
I never even dreamed you were paying
for my treatment as a host bar escort.

189
00:17:10,415 --> 00:17:14,248
Gyu O, really...

190
00:17:15,601 --> 00:17:17,441
I'm telling you, that woman is crazy.

191
00:17:17,495 --> 00:17:20,156
She knew you were the nicest guy
in the world...

192
00:17:20,181 --> 00:17:22,081
Why would you pay
for this jerk's treatment?

193
00:17:30,881 --> 00:17:35,948
Aren't you that loser Song Su Chan?

194
00:17:36,215 --> 00:17:39,315
Why did you work as a host bar escort
to pay for this jerk's treatment?

195
00:17:39,581 --> 00:17:42,615
Hey, Su Chan. I was wrong.

196
00:17:42,815 --> 00:17:46,181
I was young and immature back then.
I guess I lost my mind for a bit.

197
00:17:46,681 --> 00:17:50,415
Come on, that's why Gyu O
beat me half to death.

198
00:17:51,981 --> 00:17:56,317
So put in a good word for me with Gyu O.

199
00:17:57,815 --> 00:17:59,264
You should've told me.

200
00:17:59,491 --> 00:18:03,231
You should've told me what happened
to you when you tried to save me.

201
00:18:03,448 --> 00:18:05,493
I didn't know anything for eight years.

202
00:18:05,814 --> 00:18:07,700
I didn't know a thing.

203
00:18:20,115 --> 00:18:21,548
You should've told me. Told me!

204
00:18:21,715 --> 00:18:25,481
You should've told me you ruined your life
trying to save me, you jerk.

205
00:18:41,215 --> 00:18:42,615
You jerk.

206
00:19:06,881 --> 00:19:11,215
Hey, you jerk! Where do you think
you're going? Hey!

207
00:19:35,881 --> 00:19:37,715
I heard Han Gyu O went off the grid?

208
00:19:38,415 --> 00:19:41,215
See? I told you you couldn't handle him.

209
00:19:41,848 --> 00:19:44,715
How could you handle a guy
who's like a flopping raw fish?

210
00:19:45,848 --> 00:19:47,848
What's it to you?
It's not like I'm eating him raw.

211
00:19:50,681 --> 00:19:53,144
I'll give you your money back,
so send me your account number.

212
00:19:53,265 --> 00:19:55,825
Han Gyu O. I'm not selling him to you.

213
00:19:55,945 --> 00:19:59,948
Is Han Gyu O a flatfish at the market?
Or a rockfish?

214
00:20:02,448 --> 00:20:06,935
If you keep getting on my nerves,
I might just finish you off.

215
00:20:07,048 --> 00:20:10,381
I could post on your school's intranet
that you stole someone's man.

216
00:20:10,621 --> 00:20:13,687
And that you even paid for him.
I could post that in a heartbeat.

217
00:20:13,748 --> 00:20:16,281
You've really lost it, haven't you?

218
00:20:16,315 --> 00:20:21,115
Yes, so give me back Han Gyu O.
Han Gyu O is mine.

219
00:20:24,681 --> 00:20:30,056
If you get on my nerves one more time,
I might just call my brother-in-law.

220
00:20:30,215 --> 00:20:33,681
What? Who? Your brother-in-law?

221
00:20:33,781 --> 00:20:37,581
Yes, Han Gyu O's brother,
which makes him my brother-in-law.

222
00:20:37,615 --> 00:20:39,148
You even met Han Gyu O's brother?

223
00:20:39,248 --> 00:20:42,281
Yes, I did. So it's game over.

224
00:20:44,515 --> 00:20:46,948
You're dating Han Gyu O, not his brother.

225
00:20:48,848 --> 00:20:54,748
Han Gyu O will believe anything
his brother tells him. Happy?

226
00:20:57,581 --> 00:20:59,151
Then prove it.

227
00:21:00,192 --> 00:21:03,678
Bring Han Gyu O's brother
right in front of me.

228
00:21:10,248 --> 00:21:11,348
Brother-in-law.

229
00:21:16,148 --> 00:21:17,181
Sit here.

230
00:21:23,048 --> 00:21:25,748
Hui Na says you're her brother-in-law,
Gyu Seo.

231
00:21:29,048 --> 00:21:30,748
I think that's going a bit too far.

232
00:21:35,548 --> 00:21:36,781
He says it's going too far.

233
00:21:41,081 --> 00:21:42,881
Hui Na dumped Gyu O first.

234
00:21:43,381 --> 00:21:47,148
She stood him up and turned him down,
so he dated me instead.

235
00:21:47,348 --> 00:21:52,381
She didn't want him but wouldn't let
anyone have him, so she lured him back.

236
00:21:53,081 --> 00:21:54,115
Is that true, Ms. Kwon?

237
00:21:54,148 --> 00:21:56,348
No, that's not...

238
00:21:56,381 --> 00:21:58,515
Did you stand my brother up
and dump him, Ms. Kwon?

239
00:21:59,519 --> 00:22:02,915
Well, I mean...

240
00:22:03,048 --> 00:22:04,981
My family is super rich.

241
00:22:05,815 --> 00:22:11,315
About 100 times richer than Kwon Hui Na's?
No, more like 1,000 times richer.

242
00:22:11,548 --> 00:22:15,715
I have three cars of my own,
a vacation home on Jeju Island,

243
00:22:15,915 --> 00:22:18,848
and a 230-square-meter apartment
in Gangnam in my name.

244
00:22:19,548 --> 00:22:24,148
When my mom passes and I inherit,
Han Gyu O won't ever need to work.

245
00:22:24,315 --> 00:22:26,215
You too, Gyu Seo.

246
00:22:27,881 --> 00:22:30,748
If you want, I can even send you
to study abroad.

247
00:22:31,215 --> 00:22:34,381
Hey, is that your money?
It's your mom's money.

248
00:22:34,448 --> 00:22:39,481
Kwon Hui Na lives in a studio and has
100,000 dollars in overdraft debt.

249
00:22:40,281 --> 00:22:46,081
Her dad went broke, so the whole family
rents a 60-square-meter place out of town.

250
00:22:48,748 --> 00:22:50,581
You little...

251
00:22:54,815 --> 00:22:59,681
Gyu Seo, Han Gyu O is dating me,

252
00:22:59,881 --> 00:23:02,415
not my family.

253
00:23:05,748 --> 00:23:06,848
Go on.

254
00:23:08,475 --> 00:23:10,775
Her brother got fired and has no job.

255
00:23:11,081 --> 00:23:14,848
So even after she marries,
she'll have to pay off her dad's debts.

256
00:23:15,115 --> 00:23:19,216
If Han Gyu O marries her,
he'll spend his life paying off debt.

257
00:23:22,448 --> 00:23:27,381
That's so low. You cheap, nasty little...

258
00:23:37,281 --> 00:23:42,281
But why would someone as amazing
as you want to see my brother?

259
00:23:43,015 --> 00:23:47,615
He's a high school dropout
with no real job and no savings.

260
00:23:48,648 --> 00:23:53,090
Because he's handsome?
You plan to live off his looks?

261
00:23:54,748 --> 00:23:59,148
Yes, I'm going to live off his looks.
So what?

262
00:23:59,215 --> 00:24:01,315
What if he gets old and ugly?

263
00:24:03,481 --> 00:24:07,515
Well, if he gets ugly...

264
00:24:07,581 --> 00:24:08,881
Then you'd dump him right away.

265
00:24:09,148 --> 00:24:14,148
No, you'd dump him the moment
you got bored, before he even got old.

266
00:24:14,615 --> 00:24:16,815
Cruelly and ruthlessly,
just like you dumped your friend just now.

267
00:24:17,715 --> 00:24:19,348
Look here, Han Gyu Seo.

268
00:24:20,648 --> 00:24:23,415
My brother says he doesn't need
anything else either. Just her face.

269
00:24:23,648 --> 00:24:27,548
He doesn't care if she's rich or poor.
He'll just live off her looks too.

270
00:24:27,781 --> 00:24:32,215
And he says Ms. Kwon is the prettiest
person he's ever seen.

271
00:24:33,115 --> 00:24:36,448
His eyesight is so bad he won't notice
even when she gets old and ugly.

272
00:24:37,281 --> 00:24:39,681
He says he'll never get LASIK
or wear glasses till the day he dies.

273
00:24:40,681 --> 00:24:41,981
My brother's so weird, right?

274
00:24:58,315 --> 00:24:59,348
Ms. Kwon.

275
00:25:03,381 --> 00:25:05,015
I'll get you a taxi, Ms. Kwon.

276
00:25:06,415 --> 00:25:08,148
Tell me your address, sister-in-law.

277
00:25:12,381 --> 00:25:15,981
What did you just call me?

278
00:25:16,915 --> 00:25:21,648
Your address.
Tell me your address, sister-in-law.

279
00:25:28,981 --> 00:25:30,081
Hurry.

280
00:25:44,115 --> 00:25:45,148
Gyu Rim.

281
00:25:48,381 --> 00:25:51,981
Han Gyu Rim, Gyu Rim.

282
00:26:01,015 --> 00:26:02,048
Did I fall asleep?

283
00:26:03,248 --> 00:26:06,548
Yes, for about 20 minutes.
You must've been really tired.

284
00:26:08,248 --> 00:26:11,648
Was I snoring, by any chance?

285
00:26:13,381 --> 00:26:15,415
Just a little.

286
00:26:17,515 --> 00:26:21,881
Gyeol says when I sleep,
I snore, my mouth falls open,

287
00:26:22,015 --> 00:26:25,048
I drool, and I grind my teeth too.

288
00:26:27,581 --> 00:26:29,415
That can happen when you're stressed.

289
00:26:29,448 --> 00:26:32,615
No, he says the person next to me
can't even sleep.

290
00:26:32,715 --> 00:26:36,381
I yell in my sleep too,
and one day when I woke up,

291
00:26:36,448 --> 00:26:39,015
I was sleeping facedown
on the bathroom floor like this.

292
00:26:41,548 --> 00:26:42,915
Do I sleepwalk too?

293
00:26:44,715 --> 00:26:47,181
If you're worried,
want to go see a doctor?

294
00:26:47,348 --> 00:26:51,581
What? No. Maybe if it gets worse.

295
00:26:54,615 --> 00:26:56,881
I am a little worried, though.

296
00:26:58,081 --> 00:27:02,615
You used to sleep like Sleeping Beauty...

297
00:27:03,015 --> 00:27:05,548
without making a single sound.

298
00:27:08,648 --> 00:27:11,915
Unbelievable.

299
00:27:12,681 --> 00:27:16,448
- What?
- You've seen Sleeping Beauty sleep?

300
00:27:16,581 --> 00:27:20,948
If that's how it is, don't date me.
Go date Sleeping Beauty.

301
00:27:23,081 --> 00:27:27,315
It's kind of annoying.
This is unbelievable.

302
00:27:27,348 --> 00:27:30,281
You looked like a princess today too.

303
00:27:30,321 --> 00:27:32,400
This is really bad.

304
00:27:33,021 --> 00:27:35,721
That just makes me madder.

305
00:27:46,515 --> 00:27:49,281
Can wine really taste this different?

306
00:27:49,915 --> 00:27:53,315
I'm in trouble. I've ruined my palate.

307
00:27:54,348 --> 00:27:56,381
Before I had the wine Mu Jin gave me,

308
00:27:56,515 --> 00:28:00,715
even 15-dollar wine tasted great.
I couldn't get enough of it.

309
00:28:01,281 --> 00:28:04,379
This is trouble. What do I do?

310
00:28:07,881 --> 00:28:12,981
Who are you?
What are you doing with my wine...

311
00:28:15,448 --> 00:28:16,515
Gyu Rim?

312
00:28:28,948 --> 00:28:29,981
What?

313
00:28:48,148 --> 00:28:52,115
So embarrassing. I'm so ashamed.

314
00:28:59,815 --> 00:29:03,981
I did everything you told me to.
Is this right?

315
00:29:04,515 --> 00:29:08,581
Are you sure doing this will make him
sick of me and lose interest?

316
00:29:26,181 --> 00:29:27,848
What's wrong with Han Gyu Rim?

317
00:29:30,181 --> 00:29:32,148
Did she get shot in the head?

318
00:29:33,115 --> 00:29:37,115
Watch your mouth.
She might be my wife someday.

319
00:29:37,181 --> 00:29:42,193
You saw her like that today,
and you're fine with it?

320
00:29:42,748 --> 00:29:46,281
If I were you, I'd be so turned off
I'd never want to see her again.

321
00:29:46,915 --> 00:29:48,381
She just seemed cute and pretty.

322
00:29:48,981 --> 00:29:50,481
Get a grip, you idiot.

323
00:29:50,615 --> 00:29:54,914
Forget her embarrassing herself today.
She totally humiliated you.

324
00:29:55,081 --> 00:29:59,215
She told everyone she's your girlfriend,
like she'd planned it all along...

325
00:30:00,381 --> 00:30:02,148
I never thought she'd do that, seriously.

326
00:30:05,048 --> 00:30:08,215
Right, she meant to.

327
00:30:09,781 --> 00:30:11,348
Gyu Rim did it on purpose.

328
00:30:11,515 --> 00:30:14,181
That's what I'm saying.
She did this totally on purpose.

329
00:30:15,081 --> 00:30:16,848
What was Gyu Rim trying to do?

330
00:30:16,981 --> 00:30:19,281
I just told you. To humiliate you.

331
00:30:19,315 --> 00:30:20,715
And what would humiliating me get her?

332
00:30:20,781 --> 00:30:24,348
What would she get by humiliating you?

333
00:30:25,681 --> 00:30:28,381
Okay, that's enough.

334
00:30:29,648 --> 00:30:32,215
My head was a bit of a mess today...

335
00:30:33,615 --> 00:30:36,648
but you made me realize something.
Thank you.

336
00:30:36,748 --> 00:30:38,848
I'll buy you a drink sometime soon.

337
00:30:39,948 --> 00:30:42,348
You do come in handy sometimes.

338
00:30:43,248 --> 00:30:47,881
On purpose. Right, she did it on purpose.

339
00:30:52,015 --> 00:30:54,281
What did you realize? What was it?

340
00:30:55,015 --> 00:30:57,048
What did I say to him?

341
00:31:34,715 --> 00:31:40,348
SOS! Gyu Yeong, I think your sister
has a terminal illness.

342
00:31:41,644 --> 00:31:43,118
What is he talking about?

343
00:31:48,458 --> 00:31:50,575
- Hey, Gyu Yeong.
- What is this about?

344
00:31:50,600 --> 00:31:52,060
If you're going to lie,
make it believable.

345
00:31:52,933 --> 00:31:55,538
Gyu Rim is acting weird. Really weird.

346
00:31:55,624 --> 00:31:57,545
She's dressed like a hunter,

347
00:31:57,794 --> 00:32:01,987
wearing something like tiger skin
as hot pants and as a headband,

348
00:32:02,065 --> 00:32:06,279
and her makeup is super heavy,
with earrings dangling everywhere.

349
00:32:07,278 --> 00:32:08,563
Why would she do that?

350
00:32:09,685 --> 00:32:11,265
She's changed.

351
00:32:12,231 --> 00:32:14,318
They say people die
when they suddenly change.

352
00:32:14,811 --> 00:32:17,591
- Han Gyu Rim?
- Yes, Han Gyu Rim, your sister.

353
00:32:17,965 --> 00:32:20,378
At first, I didn't even recognize her.

354
00:32:22,004 --> 00:32:23,004
Have you been drinking?

355
00:32:24,071 --> 00:32:25,071
A little wine.

356
00:32:25,410 --> 00:32:27,704
I'm not saying this because I'm drunk.

357
00:32:29,118 --> 00:32:30,829
Just go to bed.

358
00:32:30,831 --> 00:32:33,779
If you ever scare me like this again,
I'll block your number.

359
00:32:33,960 --> 00:32:34,960
Consider yourself warned.

360
00:32:34,978 --> 00:32:37,383
Hey, are you treating me like a drunk?

361
00:32:37,385 --> 00:32:40,166
If you can't help me when
I'm working hard at my marriage,

362
00:32:40,301 --> 00:32:42,018
at least stop bothering me.

363
00:32:42,138 --> 00:32:43,938
Please, Mr. Han Seok Jung!

364
00:32:52,552 --> 00:32:55,990
I called you because I had no one else
to talk to about this,

365
00:32:56,437 --> 00:32:57,618
you cold-hearted girl.

366
00:32:58,098 --> 00:33:01,140
If I ever call you again, call me a dog.

367
00:33:01,173 --> 00:33:03,219
- Who are you blaming?
- You scared me!

368
00:33:03,771 --> 00:33:04,771
You scared me.

369
00:33:06,045 --> 00:33:08,438
Your daughter's not to blame at all.

370
00:33:08,798 --> 00:33:10,837
If you really want to blame someone,

371
00:33:11,132 --> 00:33:15,187
look in the mirror, after the way
you've lived your life.

372
00:33:16,005 --> 00:33:18,351
If you're standing behind me,
you should say so.

373
00:33:18,352 --> 00:33:23,780
The bomb that was inside Gyu Rim
just went off.

374
00:33:24,038 --> 00:33:26,891
- What?
- Back in the 1960s,

375
00:33:26,892 --> 00:33:30,576
girls who'd lost it walked around
with flowers in their hair.

376
00:33:31,798 --> 00:33:36,565
At least Gyu Rim hasn't put
a flower in her hair yet.

377
00:33:36,762 --> 00:33:40,338
She hasn't put a flower in her hair,
but she wore a tiger headband.

378
00:33:40,497 --> 00:33:43,583
I think I know why.

379
00:33:50,617 --> 00:33:53,935
Am I some puppy that follows along
whenever she tells me to?

380
00:34:00,431 --> 00:34:02,431
Gyu Rim's mom came to the side dish shop?

381
00:34:02,858 --> 00:34:05,657
I wasn't there myself,

382
00:34:05,842 --> 00:34:10,511
but she was obviously her mom,
and she acted like she wasn't,

383
00:34:10,599 --> 00:34:13,538
then just tossed her a lunch box and left.

384
00:34:13,563 --> 00:34:16,278
Why did she come
if she wasn't going to admit it?

385
00:34:16,625 --> 00:34:17,844
And what's with the lunch box?

386
00:34:18,245 --> 00:34:21,105
Did she think we couldn't even afford
a lunch box, so she tossed one over?

387
00:34:21,106 --> 00:34:22,206
That's what I'm saying.

388
00:34:23,476 --> 00:34:28,365
Gyu Rim chased after her too late,
screaming loud enough to shake the world,

389
00:34:28,513 --> 00:34:32,057
"Mom!"

390
00:34:33,336 --> 00:34:35,586
She kept calling out to her,

391
00:34:35,728 --> 00:34:37,542
and it was heartbreaking...

392
00:34:38,028 --> 00:34:41,938
If I knew her number,
I'd have given her a piece of my mind...

393
00:34:41,939 --> 00:34:44,232
That wretched woman!

394
00:34:46,191 --> 00:34:48,961
I have her number!

395
00:34:49,265 --> 00:34:53,110
Last time she came, she told me to call
if I wanted to move to the countryside.

396
00:34:54,305 --> 00:34:55,751
That wretched woman, really.

397
00:34:56,131 --> 00:34:57,411
Here's your meat.

398
00:34:57,551 --> 00:34:59,064
- Thank you.
- Enjoy.

399
00:34:59,089 --> 00:35:00,553
- Thank you!
- Sure.

400
00:35:15,077 --> 00:35:16,995
Busy! What is it?

401
00:35:17,093 --> 00:35:21,884
Even her texts are ice-cold.

402
00:35:22,980 --> 00:35:25,398
I need to hit her back too.

403
00:35:25,752 --> 00:35:26,752
What should I say?

404
00:35:27,142 --> 00:35:32,111
Should I tell her Gyu Rim put flowers
in her hair because of her?

405
00:35:32,818 --> 00:35:38,238
She could put flowers in her hair
a million times just because of you.

406
00:35:42,244 --> 00:35:44,687
Why did you just toss her a lunch box...

407
00:35:45,295 --> 00:35:47,258
and leave without telling Gyu Rim
you're her mom?

408
00:35:47,598 --> 00:35:50,139
"Mom!"

409
00:35:50,777 --> 00:35:54,488
Tell her Gyu Rim wailed,
screaming her lungs out.

410
00:35:54,852 --> 00:35:56,263
Write that too.

411
00:35:59,265 --> 00:36:00,897
Why did you just toss her a lunch box...

412
00:36:01,104 --> 00:36:03,018
and leave without telling Gyu Rim
you're her mom?

413
00:36:05,265 --> 00:36:07,175
Why did you come if you weren't
even going to admit it?

414
00:36:07,624 --> 00:36:08,758
And what's with the lunch box?

415
00:36:09,478 --> 00:36:12,284
Did you think we couldn't even afford
a lunch box, so you tossed one over?

416
00:36:13,471 --> 00:36:15,917
Hey, after you left, Gyu Rim...

417
00:36:16,018 --> 00:36:19,898
screamed "Mom!" at the top
of her lungs and wailed.

418
00:36:21,713 --> 00:36:23,518
What a thick-skinned person.

419
00:36:25,605 --> 00:36:28,151
Thick, all right. Thick as steel.

420
00:36:28,811 --> 00:36:31,439
No motherly love, no humanity,

421
00:36:31,794 --> 00:36:35,752
and not even a toenail's worth
of respect for her husband.

422
00:36:35,753 --> 00:36:38,160
I mean your skin.

423
00:36:39,845 --> 00:36:41,784
My skin isn't thick.

424
00:36:42,404 --> 00:36:44,038
My skin is so delicate,

425
00:36:45,065 --> 00:36:46,965
you have no idea how easily I break out.

426
00:36:47,598 --> 00:36:52,044
Who made Gyu Rim's mom like that?

427
00:36:52,645 --> 00:36:55,249
- You kept your wife from being a mom.
- "You kept your wife from being a mom."

428
00:36:55,274 --> 00:36:57,170
- Who kicked her out like that?
- "Who kicked her out like that?"

429
00:36:57,711 --> 00:37:00,291
- Isn't it all your fault?
- "Isn't it all your fault?"

430
00:37:00,292 --> 00:37:01,737
What are you doing?

431
00:37:01,831 --> 00:37:03,679
I've heard it so many times,

432
00:37:03,681 --> 00:37:05,061
I know what you'll say next, ma'am,

433
00:37:05,062 --> 00:37:07,944
right down to the last word.

434
00:37:08,885 --> 00:37:11,717
Fine, aren't you something.

435
00:37:14,197 --> 00:37:18,725
But are you really blameless, ma'am?

436
00:37:19,505 --> 00:37:20,505
What?

437
00:37:20,998 --> 00:37:26,140
You gave my Gyu Rim a hard time
for dumping Heung Sik.

438
00:37:26,664 --> 00:37:28,978
That was ages ago.

439
00:37:29,517 --> 00:37:33,206
I made up with Gyu Rim a long time ago,

440
00:37:33,428 --> 00:37:36,445
and we're very close now, I'm telling you.

441
00:37:37,058 --> 00:37:39,339
That's what you think.

442
00:37:39,613 --> 00:37:41,554
The way I see it, for Gyu Rim
to end up this strange,

443
00:37:41,555 --> 00:37:44,464
everyone had a hand in it.

444
00:37:46,011 --> 00:37:49,978
If you think you're blameless,
go ahead and cast the first stone.

445
00:38:00,457 --> 00:38:01,524
Why'd you hit me?

446
00:38:01,907 --> 00:38:07,562
Blameless or not, I've got to flick
that smug head of yours.

447
00:38:07,587 --> 00:38:09,485
- Want another one?
- No, thanks.

448
00:38:09,891 --> 00:38:12,191
- What are you doing?
- Where do you think you're going?

449
00:38:12,216 --> 00:38:14,318
- I said no!
- You need one more, I'm telling you.

450
00:38:33,398 --> 00:38:34,788
We agreed to fend for ourselves,

451
00:38:35,242 --> 00:38:37,324
so why are you doing everyone's laundry?

452
00:38:38,218 --> 00:38:40,673
Right? No wonder there was so much.

453
00:38:42,964 --> 00:38:44,238
Have you been drinking?

454
00:38:47,597 --> 00:38:51,594
I guess I'm a little drunk.
I drank too fast.

455
00:38:51,774 --> 00:38:54,670
- I was embarrassed.
- About what?

456
00:38:56,516 --> 00:38:57,658
Just because.

457
00:38:59,185 --> 00:39:02,118
Since when do you know how to do this?

458
00:39:02,143 --> 00:39:03,593
You used to do it for me.

459
00:39:05,342 --> 00:39:08,624
I think it's working, Doctor.

460
00:39:11,618 --> 00:39:13,394
I choked on something yesterday too,

461
00:39:13,842 --> 00:39:17,135
and some lady rubbed my back like this.

462
00:39:18,278 --> 00:39:20,198
And it felt exactly like you.

463
00:39:21,178 --> 00:39:22,391
Exactly the same as you.

464
00:39:24,130 --> 00:39:25,531
What lady?

465
00:39:26,824 --> 00:39:29,118
Just someone. A lady I know.

466
00:39:31,771 --> 00:39:32,771
Gyu Seo.

467
00:39:34,493 --> 00:39:38,264
What kind of woman do you find
the most annoying in the world?

468
00:39:38,810 --> 00:39:40,430
A woman so scary you're afraid
she'll show up in your dreams.

469
00:39:41,465 --> 00:39:43,791
Can you give me a specific example?

470
00:39:50,258 --> 00:39:52,411
Sorry I got mad earlier.

471
00:39:55,304 --> 00:39:57,169
It's okay. I understand.

472
00:40:10,171 --> 00:40:12,544
As an apology, I'm sending you a video.

473
00:40:13,053 --> 00:40:14,365
Watch it when you're alone.

474
00:40:14,745 --> 00:40:16,425
- Sweet dreams.
- What's this?

475
00:40:18,180 --> 00:40:21,820
Is anyone there? Please help me.

476
00:40:40,865 --> 00:40:43,640
- Hello?
- Jeong Woo, where are you right now?

477
00:40:44,382 --> 00:40:46,378
Hey, come quick. Come now.

478
00:40:46,379 --> 00:40:47,692
Come right now. Hurry.

479
00:40:47,838 --> 00:40:49,182
What's wrong with you?

480
00:40:49,185 --> 00:40:52,253
If the elevator doesn't come down,
just take the stairs. Hurry.

481
00:40:52,278 --> 00:40:55,619
- What? Did you see a ghost?
- Yes, I just saw a ghost.

482
00:40:55,644 --> 00:41:00,278
What do I do? I'm so scared.
Don't hang up.

483
00:41:04,958 --> 00:41:06,945
Gyu Rim, Mu Jin is here.

484
00:41:07,018 --> 00:41:10,014
He brought bread, soup, salad,
and a ton of food.

485
00:41:11,854 --> 00:41:14,224
He says he'll make breakfast. Come quick.

486
00:41:19,540 --> 00:41:23,131
Did you make all of this yourself?

487
00:41:23,156 --> 00:41:25,330
- You even baked the bread?
- Yes.

488
00:41:25,523 --> 00:41:28,140
It feels like our house is a restaurant.

489
00:41:29,158 --> 00:41:30,258
Eat up, Gyeol.

490
00:41:30,591 --> 00:41:32,571
You especially need to eat
lots of salad, okay?

491
00:41:32,596 --> 00:41:33,638
Okay.

492
00:41:33,711 --> 00:41:37,006
You brought plates, forks, knives,
and even spoons?

493
00:41:37,031 --> 00:41:39,377
Yes. I brewed some coffee too.

494
00:41:39,697 --> 00:41:40,837
I'll get it.

495
00:41:42,824 --> 00:41:44,691
It looks so good.

496
00:41:46,003 --> 00:41:48,475
- Are you here, Mu Jin?
- Yes.

497
00:41:51,270 --> 00:41:56,148
It looks really good. Thanks, Mu Jin.

498
00:41:58,671 --> 00:42:01,131
I actually had something to ask you.

499
00:42:01,344 --> 00:42:02,511
What is it?

500
00:42:03,751 --> 00:42:07,560
Our fridge is really old,
so it keeps breaking down.

501
00:42:07,811 --> 00:42:10,064
The freezer broke just a little while ago.

502
00:42:11,391 --> 00:42:13,354
Could you get me a new fridge?

503
00:42:14,497 --> 00:42:15,610
A fridge?

504
00:42:15,865 --> 00:42:17,438
We can just call a repairman.

505
00:42:18,030 --> 00:42:20,300
I'll fix it. I can fix it.

506
00:42:20,785 --> 00:42:22,391
We should buy our own fridge.

507
00:42:22,458 --> 00:42:24,178
Why ask Mu Jin to buy it?

508
00:42:24,600 --> 00:42:27,130
He could buy it for us.

509
00:42:27,491 --> 00:42:29,942
He is richer than you'd think.

510
00:42:29,944 --> 00:42:31,355
- Dad.
- Grandpa.

511
00:42:31,704 --> 00:42:34,777
Did I ask him to buy it?

512
00:42:34,925 --> 00:42:36,618
Gyu Rim asked him to.

513
00:42:37,498 --> 00:42:40,690
- Did I put too much pressure on you?
- No.

514
00:42:40,908 --> 00:42:44,114
I was thinking when I replace my fridge,
I'd get you a new one too.

515
00:42:44,116 --> 00:42:45,320
That's what I had in mind.

516
00:42:46,650 --> 00:42:50,458
How can you be so thoughtful?

517
00:42:50,598 --> 00:42:52,846
- That's not it, Dad.
- That's really not it.

518
00:42:52,871 --> 00:42:56,257
- They said that's not it, Dad.
- No means no, Grandpa.

519
00:42:56,349 --> 00:43:00,260
See? Everyone always picks on me.

520
00:43:00,285 --> 00:43:02,058
Gyu Rim's the one
who asked for the fridge.

521
00:43:02,059 --> 00:43:04,649
I didn't even say the R in "refrigerator."

522
00:43:05,269 --> 00:43:10,027
But I saw an electronics ad
a little while ago,

523
00:43:10,631 --> 00:43:16,604
and it said there's a big discount
if we swap the fridge, washer, and TV.

524
00:43:16,691 --> 00:43:17,691
Really?

525
00:43:17,880 --> 00:43:22,085
Then while we're at it, should we bundle
the washer and TV in too?

526
00:43:22,318 --> 00:43:23,947
- Dad.
- Grandpa.

527
00:43:24,618 --> 00:43:25,869
You guys, seriously!

528
00:43:25,871 --> 00:43:28,504
I was trying to stop Gyu Rim this time.

529
00:43:28,625 --> 00:43:30,044
What's wrong with you, really?

530
00:43:30,069 --> 00:43:33,134
Does Mu Jin owe you money or something?
Are we beggars?

531
00:43:33,225 --> 00:43:36,705
What if he gets sick of it and runs away?

532
00:43:37,111 --> 00:43:40,148
Why are you acting so obnoxious today?

533
00:43:40,771 --> 00:43:42,758
Mu Jin won't run away.

534
00:43:42,838 --> 00:43:46,247
He said he'd give me the moon and stars.
Why would he run away over this?

535
00:43:47,304 --> 00:43:50,187
You guys tell him
if there's anything you want. Okay?

536
00:43:50,311 --> 00:43:53,005
He is way richer than you'd think.

537
00:43:53,105 --> 00:43:56,249
So don't feel awkward, and don't be shy.

538
00:43:56,274 --> 00:43:58,935
If there's something you want,
just say so.

539
00:44:03,171 --> 00:44:04,417
Even so...

540
00:44:10,697 --> 00:44:13,757
What's wrong with Gyu Rim?
She's like a different person.

541
00:44:14,158 --> 00:44:15,704
Maybe she was joking?

542
00:44:15,798 --> 00:44:18,468
I saw it with my own eyes,
and I still can't believe it.

543
00:44:25,264 --> 00:44:27,747
- No way.
- What is it?

544
00:44:29,171 --> 00:44:32,582
This is a video and comments posted
on our restaurant's board yesterday.

545
00:44:33,600 --> 00:44:35,925
"What's with that outfit, head to toe?"

546
00:44:36,305 --> 00:44:37,964
"Does she have a grudge against tigers?"

547
00:44:39,211 --> 00:44:42,761
"Shoe on the table? Terrible manners."
"Thought it was a hidden camera prank."

548
00:44:42,991 --> 00:44:45,298
"Shouldn't a rude customer
like that be kicked out?"

549
00:44:45,331 --> 00:44:47,098
We're talking about Gyu Rim right now.

550
00:44:47,504 --> 00:44:49,318
Check your restaurant's
social media later.

551
00:44:49,343 --> 00:44:52,879
"But is she really
Chef Kim Mu Jin's girlfriend?"

552
00:44:54,144 --> 00:44:58,425
"The owner-chef's girlfriend
doesn't know vongole. So clueless."

553
00:44:58,631 --> 00:45:01,080
Is that about Gyu Rim? Give me that.

554
00:45:06,614 --> 00:45:08,860
No, this isn't Gyu Rim.

555
00:45:08,885 --> 00:45:11,065
Look closely. It's Gyu Rim.

556
00:45:16,591 --> 00:45:17,884
It's Gyu Rim, right, Gyu O?

557
00:45:18,098 --> 00:45:21,619
She was fine until last night.
Why is she suddenly like this?

558
00:45:21,644 --> 00:45:24,258
Last time, she said she lost something.

559
00:45:24,311 --> 00:45:26,218
But she said she didn't know
what she lost.

560
00:45:26,528 --> 00:45:27,724
Is it like that time?

561
00:45:27,990 --> 00:45:30,005
Did she hit her head?
Is it some kind of aftereffect?

562
00:45:35,104 --> 00:45:38,904
You were all talking about Gyu Rim, right?

563
00:45:42,944 --> 00:45:45,420
When I came home yesterday,

564
00:45:45,808 --> 00:45:48,020
with her clothes, makeup, and hair,

565
00:45:48,200 --> 00:45:50,737
I thought some strange woman
had broken into the house.

566
00:45:51,370 --> 00:45:56,365
Hey, does she remind you guys
of anyone, by any chance?

567
00:45:56,597 --> 00:46:00,775
She definitely looks like Gyu Rim,
but she talks just like someone else.

568
00:46:02,324 --> 00:46:05,487
Honestly, for a second,
I thought she was Han Gyu Yeong.

569
00:46:05,684 --> 00:46:08,447
- Me too.
- Right? You thought so too?

570
00:46:08,745 --> 00:46:12,325
I thought it was Gyu Yeong talking,
not Gyu Rim.

571
00:46:12,585 --> 00:46:14,704
It's like Gyu Yeong's spirit
got into Gyu Rim...

572
00:46:14,705 --> 00:46:16,225
What are you trying to say?

573
00:46:16,338 --> 00:46:19,998
Hey, should we hold an exorcism?

574
00:46:22,492 --> 00:46:27,103
This is just like the story in
volume eight of "I Am an Exorcist."

575
00:46:28,171 --> 00:46:33,113
The money-grubbing, man-scamming energy
in Gyu Yeong's room got into Gyu Rim...

576
00:46:33,138 --> 00:46:35,460
You brats, I'm talking here!

577
00:46:39,140 --> 00:46:43,431
What am I doing talking to high schoolers?

578
00:46:46,798 --> 00:46:47,798
Gyu O.

579
00:46:49,129 --> 00:46:53,421
What I'm saying may sound
ridiculous at first, but...

580
00:46:53,446 --> 00:46:55,904
It's ridiculous no matter how you hear it.

581
00:46:57,238 --> 00:47:00,391
Stop reading that weird comic book
and read some Nietzsche.

582
00:47:00,571 --> 00:47:02,343
Ask Mu Jin to lend you one.

583
00:47:03,871 --> 00:47:06,890
Nietzsche, my foot.
You cheeky little brat.

584
00:47:07,494 --> 00:47:09,017
Hey!

585
00:47:10,253 --> 00:47:14,271
Sisters, brothers, none of you matter!

586
00:47:15,038 --> 00:47:18,278
Nobody truly worries about Gyu Rim
except me.

587
00:47:24,815 --> 00:47:28,504
What if Mu Jin ends up dumping Gyu Rim?

588
00:47:29,845 --> 00:47:34,178
It's so hard for a single mom
to find a catch like him.

589
00:47:47,838 --> 00:47:50,280
- Mom.
- Yes?

590
00:47:51,065 --> 00:47:52,246
What's wrong with you?

591
00:47:54,018 --> 00:47:55,018
What do you mean?

592
00:47:55,340 --> 00:47:59,515
Mom. You're acting really weird today.

593
00:48:00,381 --> 00:48:01,968
You really don't know?

594
00:48:05,251 --> 00:48:06,251
I know.

595
00:48:07,092 --> 00:48:10,403
I know, but let's just let it go.

596
00:48:11,198 --> 00:48:13,204
You know you're acting weird,
and you still do it?

597
00:48:13,758 --> 00:48:16,809
You asked Mu Jin to buy you a fridge,

598
00:48:16,897 --> 00:48:18,644
and a washer too.

599
00:48:19,237 --> 00:48:23,276
I'll tell you everything later
about why I acted so strange,

600
00:48:23,758 --> 00:48:25,353
so let's just let it go today.

601
00:48:29,344 --> 00:48:31,284
Even if I told you,
you wouldn't understand.

602
00:48:32,171 --> 00:48:35,204
When you grow up,
you'll understand me too, Gyeol.

603
00:48:36,411 --> 00:48:37,951
Time for school. You're late.

604
00:48:38,551 --> 00:48:42,924
Is your goal to get rejected by Mu Jin?

605
00:48:45,298 --> 00:48:49,258
Your goal is for Mu Jin to say
he can't stand someone like you,

606
00:48:50,252 --> 00:48:54,652
and run far away, right?

607
00:48:56,677 --> 00:48:57,677
Is it obvious?

608
00:48:58,964 --> 00:49:00,925
Of course it's obvious.

609
00:49:04,791 --> 00:49:07,043
I've known Gyu Rim for a long time,

610
00:49:07,044 --> 00:49:10,778
and it's completely obvious
she's trying to push me away.

611
00:49:12,558 --> 00:49:14,214
Do I look like that much of a pushover?

612
00:49:15,098 --> 00:49:16,292
Did she think if she acted like that,

613
00:49:16,317 --> 00:49:19,769
I'd say, "I'm turned off, let's end it,"
and run away?

614
00:49:21,964 --> 00:49:23,919
What does she take me for?

615
00:49:23,971 --> 00:49:28,962
You dragged me out before I could eat,
so what is it you want to say?

616
00:49:29,421 --> 00:49:31,365
What's your point?

617
00:49:33,026 --> 00:49:36,135
The point is...

618
00:49:37,471 --> 00:49:43,611
I wanted to vent about Gyu Rim a little,
but I had no one to talk to.

619
00:49:44,165 --> 00:49:48,101
If I told Jeong Woo,
he'd take it way too seriously.

620
00:49:49,391 --> 00:49:54,548
You know, at one point,
I wanted to date Gyu Rim myself.

621
00:49:54,898 --> 00:49:58,933
That's why you came to me back then
and rubbed it in,

622
00:49:59,085 --> 00:50:01,184
saying she confessed to you and all,

623
00:50:01,258 --> 00:50:02,577
and then when you got dumped,

624
00:50:02,585 --> 00:50:05,551
asking me for tips
on how to get through being dumped.

625
00:50:05,605 --> 00:50:07,224
There's no tip for getting dumped.

626
00:50:07,358 --> 00:50:09,311
So is this your revenge?

627
00:50:10,498 --> 00:50:11,824
It's not revenge exactly.

628
00:50:15,669 --> 00:50:19,925
The way Gyu Rim keeps pushing me away,
even resorting to tricks like this,

629
00:50:19,966 --> 00:50:23,338
it kind of hurts when I think about it.

630
00:50:23,445 --> 00:50:26,511
I keep wanting to sulk at her. So...

631
00:50:28,483 --> 00:50:31,124
But why did I come to you, of all people?

632
00:50:35,531 --> 00:50:39,177
I must've lost my mind for a moment.
I'm sorry.

633
00:50:41,077 --> 00:50:44,785
If you haven't eaten yet,
can I buy you breakfast?

634
00:50:45,971 --> 00:50:49,331
Honestly, it's a shame to keep this
to myself. Such a waste.

635
00:50:49,371 --> 00:50:52,724
You look like a model student,
all clean-cut,

636
00:50:53,098 --> 00:50:56,231
so people would never guess
you're such a nutcase.

637
00:50:57,890 --> 00:50:59,591
Come on, let's eat.

638
00:50:59,592 --> 00:51:01,652
The bean sprout soup here is good.

639
00:51:03,430 --> 00:51:04,854
Well, I guess...

640
00:51:05,463 --> 00:51:09,612
I've seen love turn a man into
a lunatic overnight more than once.

641
00:51:12,779 --> 00:51:16,074
If Gyu Rim's trying to push you away,

642
00:51:16,099 --> 00:51:19,175
she must have her reasons,

643
00:51:19,920 --> 00:51:24,288
so be a man about it and give her up.

644
00:51:25,911 --> 00:51:29,266
What? Give her up?

645
00:51:29,408 --> 00:51:31,798
You said you were rooting
for us back then.

646
00:51:31,799 --> 00:51:35,512
I was.
I rooted for you with all my heart...

647
00:51:36,670 --> 00:51:40,564
That was before I knew you were
the only son of a conglomerate family.

648
00:51:42,704 --> 00:51:47,437
If you were the youngest son,
or even the second son,

649
00:51:47,672 --> 00:51:50,958
I'd have taken your side
and told you to go for it.

650
00:51:52,784 --> 00:51:55,855
You cut ties with your mother
because of Gyu Rim,

651
00:51:55,880 --> 00:51:58,811
and you walked away
from your whole fortune, right?

652
00:51:58,836 --> 00:52:00,116
Yes.

653
00:52:01,537 --> 00:52:04,204
Can you imagine how much pressure
that puts on Gyu Rim?

654
00:52:04,390 --> 00:52:07,483
It's not like Gyu Rim's crazy about
luxury goods like Gyu Yeong,

655
00:52:07,508 --> 00:52:09,968
or would do anything for money.

656
00:52:10,065 --> 00:52:12,992
For someone like her, making you a bad son
to your mother would be torture,

657
00:52:13,017 --> 00:52:15,479
like sitting on a bed of thorns.

658
00:52:15,616 --> 00:52:18,244
Why would she want a marriage like that?

659
00:52:18,309 --> 00:52:24,183
So the only son of a conglomerate family
can't marry the woman he loves?

660
00:52:24,924 --> 00:52:27,360
Isn't this reverse discrimination?

661
00:52:27,605 --> 00:52:31,285
And she's not marrying my mother.
She's marrying me.

662
00:52:31,484 --> 00:52:34,120
The reason I gave up everything
and left home...

663
00:52:34,376 --> 00:52:39,142
is that my mother judges people
by their background, and that's wrong.

664
00:52:42,285 --> 00:52:47,052
When I hear one side, it sounds right.
When I hear the other, that's right too.

665
00:52:48,284 --> 00:52:51,363
Then I'll stay neutral.

666
00:52:51,484 --> 00:52:55,532
Not a bird, not a mouse...
I guess that makes me a bat.

667
00:52:57,050 --> 00:52:58,464
What?

668
00:53:00,091 --> 00:53:02,026
You're no help at all.

669
00:53:08,705 --> 00:53:10,851
What is this?

670
00:53:11,031 --> 00:53:13,164
How dare you do this to my face!

671
00:53:23,584 --> 00:53:29,251
Wipe it off yourself, right now,
while I'm still being nice!

672
00:53:30,890 --> 00:53:33,422
While I'm still being nice,
get this off right now.

673
00:53:33,844 --> 00:53:36,653
Let me eat too. It's already past ten.

674
00:53:36,678 --> 00:53:39,750
Is eating breakfast after ten
something to brag about?

675
00:53:40,438 --> 00:53:41,858
Mom, look at this.

676
00:53:41,859 --> 00:53:43,645
Gyu Yeong wrote this on my face...

677
00:53:43,670 --> 00:53:45,816
What is this? Son of a...

678
00:53:45,958 --> 00:53:50,218
If my son is a son of a dog,
does that make me a dog?

679
00:53:50,383 --> 00:53:53,090
Where did you learn to behave like this?

680
00:53:53,144 --> 00:53:55,110
Hey, get this off right now!

681
00:54:00,417 --> 00:54:05,370
How on earth did your family raise you?

682
00:54:07,171 --> 00:54:10,250
Hey, is this your face or mine?

683
00:54:10,275 --> 00:54:13,048
Stop looking at your phone
and clean this right now!

684
00:54:13,360 --> 00:54:15,318
You two really...

685
00:54:15,784 --> 00:54:18,224
Why won't this come off?

686
00:54:18,497 --> 00:54:23,746
Kang Seong Uk, go find something
to take off nail polish. Hurry.

687
00:54:25,898 --> 00:54:28,704
On my handsome son's face.

688
00:54:30,911 --> 00:54:34,779
Look how it's smearing red
all over my son's face.

689
00:54:34,804 --> 00:54:36,284
What is this now?

690
00:54:36,743 --> 00:54:39,897
A picture of me and Seong Uk's baby.
Eight weeks along.

691
00:54:40,031 --> 00:54:43,193
I sent it to the baby's dad too.
Doesn't Seong Uk look so happy?

692
00:54:43,218 --> 00:54:44,321
It's all smeared.

693
00:54:45,941 --> 00:54:48,715
Look at her bullying my handsome son.

694
00:54:48,756 --> 00:54:50,331
A dog, of all things.

695
00:54:50,998 --> 00:54:53,284
So handsome.

696
00:54:59,144 --> 00:55:01,257
Are you out of your mind?

697
00:55:03,991 --> 00:55:08,139
That girl is pregnant with his baby.

698
00:55:08,787 --> 00:55:10,685
Eight weeks along!

699
00:55:11,811 --> 00:55:13,044
Kang Seong Uk.

700
00:55:15,111 --> 00:55:17,211
You really are beyond saving, aren't you?

701
00:55:17,304 --> 00:55:19,937
You con artist! You filthy jerk!

702
00:55:20,656 --> 00:55:23,411
You're the one who pulled a con,
you con artist!

703
00:55:23,418 --> 00:55:24,464
Hey!

704
00:55:25,517 --> 00:55:26,901
Mom.

705
00:55:33,038 --> 00:55:36,900
Hey, did you think we wouldn't find out?

706
00:55:37,804 --> 00:55:41,504
You had a perfectly good father,
but teamed up with a conglomerate head...

707
00:55:41,529 --> 00:55:44,824
and lied that he was your father.
Did you think we wouldn't find out?

708
00:56:02,338 --> 00:56:04,604
Yes, this looks great.

709
00:56:04,895 --> 00:56:07,833
The reviewers and dealers
are responding well too, right?

710
00:56:07,930 --> 00:56:11,931
- Yes. All your hard work has paid off.
- Thank you.

711
00:56:11,951 --> 00:56:15,205
Good work. Carry on.

712
00:56:16,384 --> 00:56:17,887
Yes, sir.

713
00:56:18,185 --> 00:56:20,815
A Mr. Kang Sang Man
is in the lobby right now,

714
00:56:20,840 --> 00:56:23,711
and he says he's here to see you, sir.

715
00:56:24,364 --> 00:56:26,112
Kang Sang Man?

716
00:56:27,751 --> 00:56:29,688
Hold on, where have I heard that name?

717
00:56:30,891 --> 00:56:33,974
He said you'd know him
as Han Gyu Yeong's father-in-law...

718
00:56:37,344 --> 00:56:39,100
Kang Sang Man?

719
00:56:40,918 --> 00:56:43,044
Okay, thank you.

720
00:56:43,873 --> 00:56:47,572
I'm sorry I haven't been in touch.
It's been far too long.

721
00:56:47,598 --> 00:56:50,317
- You've been well, sir?
- Of course.

722
00:56:50,650 --> 00:56:53,268
I hear you're well known
in business circles...

723
00:56:53,476 --> 00:56:55,371
for your fine character and integrity.

724
00:56:55,386 --> 00:56:57,611
You flatter me.

725
00:56:57,636 --> 00:57:02,091
For a man of such principle,
your conscience must've weighed on you.

726
00:57:02,558 --> 00:57:05,412
You must not have been able
to sleep soundly at night.

727
00:57:06,684 --> 00:57:08,564
What do you mean by that?

728
00:57:08,791 --> 00:57:13,338
Well, to be fair,
who in this world is without fault?

729
00:57:13,664 --> 00:57:17,456
In a way, your second wife's daughter
is still your daughter,

730
00:57:17,551 --> 00:57:20,667
and the man who married her mother
is still her father,

731
00:57:20,747 --> 00:57:23,219
so it's not a complete con, is it?

732
00:57:23,867 --> 00:57:25,223
A con?

733
00:57:29,864 --> 00:57:31,324
What is it you want?

734
00:57:39,144 --> 00:57:41,637
Lend me some money for my business, sir.

735
00:57:50,925 --> 00:57:52,582
Here's your meat.

736
00:57:56,071 --> 00:58:00,023
Enjoy, and let me know
if you need anything.

737
00:58:00,170 --> 00:58:03,211
- Thank you.
- Thank you, this looks great.

738
00:58:14,431 --> 00:58:16,365
Are you a fan of mine, by any chance?

739
00:58:16,518 --> 00:58:17,818
Do I look like an electric fan?

740
00:58:17,843 --> 00:58:20,444
No, I mean, are you my fan?

741
00:58:20,675 --> 00:58:22,588
Give me your phone.
I'll take a picture with you.

742
00:58:23,684 --> 00:58:27,655
I'm not a fan.
I just needed somewhere to hide...

743
00:58:29,197 --> 00:58:31,490
Could you just stand in front of me
for a second?

744
00:58:35,436 --> 00:58:39,379
My mom's over there,
and I'll be in trouble if she sees me.

745
00:58:40,278 --> 00:58:41,971
Who's your mom?

746
00:58:43,565 --> 00:58:45,090
The server with the bob.

747
00:58:53,323 --> 00:58:57,563
(Damga Charcoal Grill)

748
00:59:00,858 --> 00:59:03,217
Gyu Seo?

749
00:59:04,044 --> 00:59:05,439
Hello.

750
00:59:09,357 --> 00:59:12,371
This is my girlfriend. She's a little shy.

751
00:59:14,938 --> 00:59:16,344
Are you here for barbecue?

752
00:59:16,369 --> 00:59:17,835
If so, why not come in?

753
00:59:17,860 --> 00:59:19,496
No, I was just passing by.

754
00:59:20,354 --> 00:59:24,934
These are called citron rice cakes.
They say kings used to eat them.

755
00:59:25,144 --> 00:59:27,617
A fan of mine gave them to me.
Her mom made them herself.

756
00:59:27,671 --> 00:59:30,204
Why give me something so special?

757
00:59:30,678 --> 00:59:32,600
You should take it home to your dad.

758
00:59:32,771 --> 00:59:35,025
Or share it with your girlfriend.

759
00:59:35,678 --> 00:59:38,281
My dad and my girlfriend
don't really like rice cakes...

760
00:59:41,085 --> 00:59:43,348
Thank you, then. I'll enjoy them.

761
00:59:43,963 --> 00:59:45,805
I'm a little busy right now...

762
00:59:45,927 --> 00:59:47,876
Come by for barbecue next time, okay?

763
00:59:48,271 --> 00:59:50,124
Bring your girlfriend too.

764
00:59:51,458 --> 00:59:53,834
Let me see your face next time.

765
00:59:55,418 --> 00:59:56,937
I'll enjoy them.

766
01:00:01,345 --> 01:00:02,845
That lady is your mom?

767
01:00:13,865 --> 01:00:15,544
Why are you hiding from your mom?

768
01:00:18,104 --> 01:00:20,391
What's your relationship with my mom?

769
01:00:20,651 --> 01:00:22,297
I asked you first.

770
01:00:22,457 --> 01:00:24,143
I even hid you so she wouldn't see you.

771
01:00:26,203 --> 01:00:28,853
I'm thirsty. Want some water?

772
01:00:29,817 --> 01:00:31,655
Why are you hiding from your mom?

773
01:00:33,781 --> 01:00:36,976
- High schooler?
- Yes.

774
01:00:37,944 --> 01:00:40,199
Why do you think I'd hide from my mom?

775
01:00:40,224 --> 01:00:41,945
Because I don't want to run into her.

776
01:00:42,417 --> 01:00:44,303
Did your mom abandon you or something?

777
01:00:45,944 --> 01:00:47,084
What are you talking about?

778
01:00:47,184 --> 01:00:49,671
Did she run off with another man
and leave you behind?

779
01:00:50,363 --> 01:00:53,074
- Hey.
- If not, why are you hiding from her?

780
01:00:53,103 --> 01:00:54,284
She's your mom.

781
01:00:54,577 --> 01:00:56,296
She seemed like a really nice lady.

782
01:00:58,019 --> 01:00:59,418
Who are you?

783
01:00:59,443 --> 01:01:00,970
How do you know my mom?

784
01:01:00,995 --> 01:01:03,081
Anyone would think you were her son.

785
01:01:03,290 --> 01:01:05,192
I wish I were her son.

786
01:01:05,725 --> 01:01:07,864
Then I could finally be
the good son I never got to be.

787
01:01:10,460 --> 01:01:12,051
Hey, who are you?

788
01:01:12,076 --> 01:01:14,685
What's your name?
What school, what grade, what class?

789
01:01:22,544 --> 01:01:26,755
I really don't have a single friend.

790
01:01:27,871 --> 01:01:29,819
Now that I've deleted Jang Hun Tae,

791
01:01:30,407 --> 01:01:33,780
I don't have a single friend
to talk to and open up to.

792
01:01:35,941 --> 01:01:38,592
Ok Seon, you've wasted your life.

793
01:01:39,223 --> 01:01:41,627
You've really wasted your life.

794
01:01:43,730 --> 01:01:48,226
My son left,

795
01:01:48,542 --> 01:01:51,091
my friend left...

796
01:01:51,624 --> 01:01:56,280
Ok Seon, what kind of life have you...

797
01:01:57,810 --> 01:02:00,497
I do. I do have a friend to call.

798
01:02:07,851 --> 01:02:10,181
Ok Seon, what's up?

799
01:02:12,991 --> 01:02:14,550
Seok Jung.

800
01:02:15,516 --> 01:02:20,133
I'm so lonely and sad right now.

801
01:02:20,898 --> 01:02:22,530
What do I do when I feel like this?

802
01:02:29,307 --> 01:02:31,159
- Seok Jung.
- What?

803
01:02:31,160 --> 01:02:33,194
- Thank you.
- For what?

804
01:02:33,219 --> 01:02:35,977
You showed me a whole new world.

805
01:02:36,078 --> 01:02:39,077
What would I have done without you
in my life?

806
01:02:39,871 --> 01:02:42,711
I'm so happy to have you too.

807
01:02:42,714 --> 01:02:43,717
Really?

808
01:02:43,718 --> 01:02:47,071
- My kids treat me like I'm useless.
- Yeah.

809
01:02:47,096 --> 01:02:50,053
You made me realize
I'm still a useful person,

810
01:02:50,090 --> 01:02:52,281
and that I'm lucky to be alive.

811
01:02:52,306 --> 01:02:54,536
- Really?
- Thank you, Ok Seon.

812
01:02:54,567 --> 01:02:58,733
You're welcome. Let's go!

813
01:02:58,758 --> 01:03:00,334
Let's roll!

814
01:03:01,111 --> 01:03:03,297
Let's go.

815
01:03:19,230 --> 01:03:22,210
Please, just dump me today, Mu Jin.

816
01:03:22,944 --> 01:03:25,583
I can't think of anything
crazier to do anymore.

817
01:03:32,304 --> 01:03:33,737
Gyu Rim.

818
01:03:43,148 --> 01:03:45,576
It's me. Mu Jin.

819
01:03:52,784 --> 01:03:54,330
Don't worry, Gyu Rim.

820
01:03:54,450 --> 01:03:56,410
I'll just become like you.

821
01:03:56,745 --> 01:04:00,358
We can be embarrassing together
and crazy together.

822
01:04:37,292 --> 01:04:39,458
(Love on the Menu)

823
01:04:39,483 --> 01:04:41,330
No matter what you do on purpose,

824
01:04:41,362 --> 01:04:43,730
I won't misunderstand,
and I won't run away.

825
01:04:43,755 --> 01:04:45,762
Make up with your mother.

826
01:04:45,787 --> 01:04:47,754
It looks like I do have a grandson...

827
01:04:47,779 --> 01:04:48,779
Hey, kiddo.

828
01:04:48,804 --> 01:04:50,519
If that fails, I'll just take my grandson.

829
01:04:50,544 --> 01:04:52,789
- Me?
- Who did you get your brains from?

830
01:04:52,814 --> 01:04:53,814
A divorce?

831
01:04:53,839 --> 01:04:55,027
Who said you could get divorced?

832
01:04:55,052 --> 01:04:56,787
Either live with me ten more years,

833
01:04:56,812 --> 01:04:58,864
- or pay me three million dollars.
- You're crazy.

834
01:04:58,889 --> 01:05:00,068
Hello.

835
01:05:00,093 --> 01:05:02,769
Han Gyu Rim came to my house?
To see our mom.

836
01:05:02,984 --> 01:05:05,667
I came to take back what I said.

837
01:05:06,869 --> 01:05:08,669
Dramaday.me
